#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""helm — mint a durable fingerprint address; resolve it onto a later tree.

A file:line is a locator. It dies when the file splits. A helm is the
fingerprint (line + identifiers + in-scope neighbors + path hint +
repo origin) so a ticket can store the address without the SHA.

v0.7 keeps shunt's leftover-as-import-pointer and keel's origin key
(remotes + tip witnesses, not root SHAs) and flips leftover matching:

  * leftover is an import *relative to the leftover file*, not an
    unanchored substring and not basename bait
  * `from .ops import add` in src/calc.py names dest src/math/ops.py
    (the extract), not sibling-only `src.ops` and not helpers.py
  * `from .calc import` names dest src/math/calc.py when that extract
    is the unique leftover-relative calc module besides the stub
  * `from src.math import calc` at module level follows
  * `io.fs` ⊂ `audio.fs` is not a pointer. Relative `.fs` that hits
    both radio/fs and io/fs stays ambiguous
  * extract-and-keep is identity if origin still holds the body
  * a missing --to ref is an error; a truncated token fails closed
  * origin is remotes + tip witnesses (keel), not sorted root SHAs
"""
